# The light debugger's body (ui::LightsPanel in client/src/ui/dev/lightspanel.cpp). The code fills "rows" (a header per group, then one row per
# term: its tick and SOLO) and the "count" line, and says what the ids do. Format: README.md here.

col gap=8 pad=10
	row size=28 gap=8
		button "ALL ON" id=all size=auto tip="Every light term and every lamp on again"
		spacer size=fill
		label id=count size=auto colour=Main alpha=0.75
	panel look=inset size=fill
		scroll id=rows x=4 y=4 w=4 h=4
	label "Tick: the term on or off. SOLO: only that term, and what it needs to show." size=auto colour=Main alpha=0.6 wrap=on
